WF-47 — Unsubscribe Handler (STOP keyword)

## Summary

- Inputs: phoneNumber, userStatus (current status of the user), userId (passed from caller WF-20)
- Outputs: users row updated to opted_out; admin_actions row inserted; opt-out confirmation WhatsApp sent; consult Slack channel archived. If user is currently in consultation_active, a hold message is sent instead and no state change occurs.
- State Transitions: any (non-consultation_active) → `opted_out`. consultation_active → no change.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-50 (Send WhatsApp) twice — once for hold message, once for opt-out confirmation.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow (typically WF-20) with { phoneNumber, userStatus, userId, ... } passed through.
Step 2: Check: userStatus equals 'consultation_active'?
  - If YES → go to Step 3
  - If NO → go to Step 4
Step 3: Call WF-50 with messageType=text, phoneNumber=<phoneNumber>, messageContent=<hold message explaining STOP cannot be processed during an active consultation>. Then go to Step 9 (End — no state change, no DB log).
Step 4: Update user status: UPDATE chinmay_astro.users SET status='opted_out', updated_at=NOW() WHERE phone_number=<phoneNumber>. Go to Step 5.
Step 5: Insert admin action: INSERT INTO chinmay_astro.admin_actions (user_id, action_type, performed_by, notes, created_at) VALUES (<userId>, 'opted_out', 'system', 'User sent STOP keyword', NOW()). Go to Step 6.
Step 6: Call WF-50 with messageType=text, phoneNumber=<phoneNumber>, messageContent=<opt-out confirmation message>. Go to Step 7.
Step 7: Look up consult channel: SELECT slack_channel_id FROM chinmay_astro.users WHERE phone_number=<phoneNumber>. Go to Step 8.
Step 8: Archive that Slack channel via Slack API (channels.archive on slack_channel_id). On error continue. Go to Step 9.
Step 9: End.
